# UX taste

- Keep a destructive action away and clearly distinguishable from the action people use most. e.g. Do not place Remove next to Schedule, or Delete next to Save.
- Confirm before a destructive action. The first click asks. The second click does it.
- Icon controls are the glyph only. No filled button behind them. A dark or solid background on an icon makes a quiet control look like a primary button.